P["Management consulting firms"] = "Buyers hire the named consultant, so individual profiles outperform firm capability pages consistently."
P["Strategy consulting firms"] = "Published thinking is the credential, and firms without a point of view compete on price."
P["Operations consulting firms"] = "Sold on measurable improvement, which means published outcomes matter more than methodology descriptions."
P["HR consulting firms"] = "Regulatory change creates urgent demand spikes that content published quickly can capture."
P["Marketing consulting firms"] = "Selling marketing means the firm's own marketing is the proof, and buyers check."
P["Technology consulting firms"] = "Vendor certifications are what buyers filter on, and each one deserves its own page."
P["Cybersecurity consulting firms"] = "Incidents drive urgent demand, and standing content ranks when the search happens."
P["Sustainability consulting firms"] = "Reporting requirements create compliance driven demand tied to regulatory deadlines."
P["Healthcare consulting firms"] = "Sector-specific credibility is the entry requirement, and generalist positioning does not clear it."
P["Government relations firms"] = "Registration and lobbying disclosure rules constrain how services can be described publicly."
P["Economic consulting firms"] = "Litigation support and policy work have different buyers, and expert witness credentials are the qualification."
P["Procurement consulting firms"] = "Sold on measurable savings, so the case for the engagement is arithmetic and should be shown as such."
P["Business brokerage firms"] = "Sellers search once in a career, so the content job is explaining valuation and process years before the sale."
P["Mergers and acquisitions advisors"] = "Deal experience by sector and size is what clients filter on, and a transaction list is the credential."

# --- Technology and managed services (12) ---
P["Managed IT service providers"] = "Contract value over years justifies an acquisition cost that looks indefensible against a first month invoice."
P["Cybersecurity companies"] = "Compliance requirements drive purchasing, and mapping services to specific frameworks is what buyers search."
P["Cloud consulting firms"] = "Platform partnership tiers are the credential buyers filter on, and each partnership deserves a page."
P["Software development companies"] = "Portfolio and technical depth carry the decision, and offshore price competition makes process the differentiator."
P["Data and analytics consultancies"] = "Buyers want to see the deliverable, so sample outputs do more than capability descriptions."
P["ERP consulting firms"] = "Implementation partner selection follows platform selection, so the marketing has to reach buyers at the right stage."
P["CRM consulting firms"] = "Adoption failure is the buyer's real fear, and addressing it directly differentiates from implementation-focused competitors."
P["Telecommunications companies"] = "Business contracts with long terms where service level agreements decide the purchase."
P["IT asset disposition companies"] = "Data destruction certification and environmental compliance are the qualifying criteria."
P["Digital transformation consultancies"] = "A vague category label, so the pages that work are built around specific outcomes rather than the term."
P["AI consulting firms"] = "A fast-moving category where demonstrated implementations matter more than claimed capability."
P["B2B SaaS companies"] = "Free trial and demo paths need separate measurement because they attract different buyer readiness."

