P["Residential real estate brokerages"] = "Individual agents market against their own brokerage, which splits budget and confuses the brand."
P["Property management companies"] = "Owners buy on reporting transparency and tenant retention, not on management fee percentage."
P["Commercial property management firms"] = "Institutional owners require reporting and compliance capability that should be documented publicly."
P["Real estate investment firms"] = "Securities regulations restrict how investment opportunities can be advertised and to whom."
P["Real estate development firms"] = "Pre-sales and investor confidence are the marketing objectives, not consumer awareness."
P["Architecture firms"] = "Selected on portfolio and project type experience, which makes the project pages the entire marketing asset."
P["Engineering firms"] = "Professional designation is legally protected and describing capability incorrectly is a regulatory issue."
P["Surveying firms"] = "Transaction and construction driven, where turnaround time is the deciding factor between firms."
P["Appraisal firms"] = "Lenders and lawyers are the referral source, so turnaround time and report acceptance are the selling points."
P["Mortgage appraisal companies"] = "Lender panel membership drives the volume, which makes this a business to business relationship business."

